course: dictionary
lesson: 13912
title: Old words, old jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A laundress is a woman whose job is to wash and iron clothes and sheets for other people. The word is old-fashioned, so you will meet it more in old books and history lessons than in everyday talk.
explain: Look at the words around it: «The laundress hung the wet sheets on the line.» Wet sheets and a line tell you she was washing, and the word for a person who does that kind of job is laundress.
explain: Many poor women worked as laundresses in Victorian and Edwardian times. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad escapes from prison disguised as a washerwoman, and later he tries washing clothes himself and makes a terrible mess. Being a laundress was hard work.
fact: A laundress is a woman who washes and irons clothes and sheets for other people.
fact: Laundress is an old-fashioned word, so it is used most in history and old stories.
fact: Laundry means clothes and sheets that need washing, and it is a word close to laundress.
fact: Many poor women worked as laundresses in Victorian and Edwardian times.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad escapes from prison disguised as a washerwoman, and later he tries washing clothes and makes a mess of it.
exercise: «The laundress ironed the sheets until they were smooth.» What is a laundress? | *A woman who washes and irons clothes for other people | A woman who sells flowers in the market | A cook who bakes bread for the family | A teacher who works at a school
exercise: Which job would a laundress do? | Mending the roof of a church | Looking after sheep on a farm | *Washing and ironing sheets for other people | Driving a horse and cart across the hills
exercise: Toad escapes from prison disguised as a washerwoman. Which word means nearly the same as washerwoman? | prisoner | gaoler | *laundress | butler
test: «Long ago, the laundress carried heavy baskets of clothes up the stairs.» What does laundress mean? | *A woman who washes and irons clothes for other people | A woman who rides a horse to work | A woman who keeps a shop | A girl who looks after young children
test: Which job would a laundress most likely be doing? | Reading a map to find the way | *Ironing a shirt for a family | Driving a bus through the town | Painting a picture of the sea
exam: «The laundress scrubbed the muddy clothes in cold water.» Which word shows what her job was? | evening | *scrubbed | muddy | window
